#TODO: Update the unit test with new Scenario
Feature: Delete Resource Type

  Background:
    Given a Resource Type for API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' with specific attributes exists
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ-D",
         "name": "FAQ-D",
         "description": "FAQ",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """
    And a Resource Type for API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' with specific attributes exists
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ-E",
         "name": "FAQ-E",
         "description": "FAQ",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ],
         "tags": [
            "tag1",
            "tag2"
         ]
      }
      """

  Scenario: Success: delete by Key
    When Resource Admin wants to delete the Resource Type with key 'FAQ-D' and API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552'
    Then the Resource Type deleted successfully with response code 204

  Scenario: Success: delete by Key with tags
    When Resource Admin wants to delete the Resource Type with key 'FAQ-E' and API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552'
    Then the Resource Type deleted successfully with response code 204

  Scenario: Success: Delete Resource with an existing/duplicate key but with different project
    Given a Resource Type for API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57722' with specific attributes exists
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ-D",
         "name": "FAQ-D",
         "description": "Frequently Asked Question Project 2",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """
    When Resource Admin wants to delete the Resource Type with key 'FAQ-D' and API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57722'
    Then the Resource Type deleted successfully with response code 204

  Scenario: Negative Delete Resource Type by a non-existent Key
    When Resource Admin wants to delete the Resource Type with key "FailKey" and API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552'
    Then the Resource Type deletion fails with response code 404
    And the response body includes status 404 and error message 'Not Found'

  Scenario: Negative Delete the Resource Type Used by Policy
    Given a Resource Type for API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' with specific attributes exists
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ-DP",
         "name": "FAQ-DP",
         "description": "FAQ Duplicate Test",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """
    * a Policy for API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' with specific attributes exists
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ_ADMIN_POLICY_USED",
         "description": "FAQ resource policy for Admin",
         "resourceType": "FAQ-DP",
         "scope": "",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ],
         "roles": [
            "ADMIN"
         ],
         "effect": "ALLOW"
      }
      """
    When Resource Admin wants to delete the Resource Type with key "FAQ-DP" and API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552'
    Then the Resource Type deletion fails with response code 409
    And the response body includes status 409 and error message 'Conflict'
